---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Divider from "../components/Divider.astro";
import StillWater from "../components/StillWater.astro";
import Seal from "../components/Seal.astro";

const DASHES = [
  "M2 6.6 C 5 5.4, 9 6.6, 13.5 5.4",
  "M2.2 6 C 5.4 6.8, 9.4 5.2, 13.8 6.2",
  "M1.8 6.4 C 5.2 5.6, 8.8 6.8, 13.4 5.8",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Biographical context, a conversion to the Church of Emacs, systems background, and open source contributions of Szymon Wilczek."
  type="profile"
>
  <header class="about-head">
    <div>
      <h1>About me</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Software engineer, <del>dualist editor enthusiast</del>
        <ins class="hand">Emacs convert</ins>, and open-source contributor.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="say hand" href="/contact/">
      <Seal glyph="文" size={40} tilt={-6} />
      <span>
        <span class="say-title">
          contact &amp; key →
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 8" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <path
              d="M1 5 C 20 3, 45 6.5, 70 4 S 92 4.5, 99 3.4"
              vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"
            ></path>
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="say-sub">mail, gpg, a postcard</span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </header>

  <Divider from={90} to={300} />

  <div class="sections">
    <section>
      <p class="num" aria-hidden="true">
        01
      </p>
      <div class="body">
        <h2>Background &amp; origins</h2>
        <p>
          I am a software engineer with academic and practical roots at the
          <strong>Silesian University of Technology</strong> (Faculty of Automatic Control,
          Electronics and Computer Science). My engineering interests lie at the intersection of
          low-level operating systems, kernel internals, and sovereign computing tools. The years so
          far, studies, work and certificates, are laid out as
          <a href="/path/">stepping stones</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything I build is pressed and labelled in <a href="/projects/">projects</a>; the rest
          of this website is my independent hypermedia space for tools, personal archives, and
          technical explorations. What I read stands on the <a href="/books/">bookshelf</a>, and
          what I work with lies on a <a href="/uses/">tea tray</a>. The whole garden is drawn on the
          <a href="/map/">map</a> if you ever get lost.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="num" aria-hidden="true">
        02
      </p>
      <div class="body">
        <h2>
          <del datetime="2026-10-12">The dualist philosophy</del>
          <ins datetime="2026-10-12">The Church of Emacs</ins>
        </h2>
        <div class="recanted">
          <p>
            Well, maybe some people would hang me for it, but in the long-standing text editor
            discourse, I <del>belong</del>
            <ins class="hand">belonged</ins> firmly to the camp of the <strong>Dualists</strong>:
          </p>
          <div class="editors">
            <div class="editor paper">
              <p class="editor-name hand emacs">GNU Emacs</p>
              <p>
                Mission control and operational headquarters. Powered by Org-mode, it drives my
                digital garden, agenda, and literate programming, with occasional Lisp.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="editor paper retired">
              <p class="editor-name hand nvim">
                <del>Neovim</del>
              </p>
              <p>
                <del>
                  My primary code-writing weapon and high-speed editing environment. I rely on it
                  for most daily programming, build custom Lua plugins, and contribute to
                  <a
                    href="https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues?q=involves:szymonwilczek"
                    rel="noopener"
                  >
                    Neovim upstream
                  </a>
                  .
                </del>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>
            <del>
              Rather than treating these tools as mutually exclusive (which most people do), I use
              the raw modal editing speed of Neovim alongside the limitless extensibility of Emacs
              to create perfect balance in the force.
            </del>
          </p>
          <p class="margin-note hand">
            left as I wrote it. I don't take back what I once believed by deleting it; this stays
            here for good.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p>
          Since then I have gone over to the <strong>Church of Emacs</strong>, one hundred percent -
          maybe it is inevitable? Since that day, the code, the garden, the agenda, all of it now
          happens in one Lisp machine. Neovim taught me a lot and my patches upstream still stand; I
          just don't use it as often anymore.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="num" aria-hidden="true">
        03
      </p>
      <div class="body">
        <h2>Upstream contributions &amp; free software</h2>
        <p>
          I believe deeply (really deeply) in the ethos of Free and Open Source Software. As a
          matter of principle, I contribute back to the projects and tools I use:
        </p>
        <ul class="dashes">
          <li>
            <svg width="16" height="12" viewBox="0 0 16 12" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d={DASHES[0]}></path>
            </svg>
            <span>
              <a href="https://lore.kernel.org/all/?q=swilczek.lx@gmail.com" rel="noopener">
                Linux kernel
              </a>
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg width="16" height="12" viewBox="0 0 16 12" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d={DASHES[1]}></path>
            </svg>
            <span>
              <a
                href="https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues?q=involves:szymonwilczek"
                rel="noopener"
              >
                Neovim
              </a>
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg width="16" height="12" viewBox="0 0 16 12" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d={DASHES[2]}></path>
            </svg>
            <span>
              <strong>Independent open source</strong> &dash; author of many tools and editor
              packages, including
              <a href="https://github.com/szymonwilczek/typus-fonts" rel="noopener">
                fonts
              </a>
              ,
              <a href="https://github.com/szymonwilczek?tab=repositories&q=nvim" rel="noopener">
                Neovim plugins
              </a>
              ,
              <a href="https://github.com/szymonwilczek?tab=repositories&q=emacs" rel="noopener">
                Emacs utilities
              </a>
              , and
              <a href="/projects">more</a>.
            </span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="num" aria-hidden="true">
        04
      </p>
      <div class="body">
        <h2>Bespoke projects &amp; repositories</h2>
        <p>
          All of my independent experiments and configurations are hosted on my
          <a href="https://github.com/szymonwilczek" rel="noopener">
            GitHub profile
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <StillWater />

  <p class="clue hand">the wolf has ten strokes.</p>
  <Seal glyph="終" size={48} tilt={3} label="end" class="about-end" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 2rem 4rem;
  }

  .about-head > div {
    flex: 999 1 32.5rem;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 42.5rem;
  }

  .about-head h1 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .lede {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1.4375rem;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
  }

  .say {
    flex: 1 1 14rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.875rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--fg-main);
    text-decoration: none;
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
  }

  .say > span {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .say-title {
    position: relative;
    width: fit-content;
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .say-title svg {
    position: absolute;
    left: -2px;
    bottom: -0.3rem;
    width: calc(100% + 4px);
    height: 0.5rem;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .say-title path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--red);
    stroke-width: 2.2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    opacity: 0.75;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .say:hover .say-title path,
  .say:focus-visible .say-title path {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .say-sub {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
  }

  .say:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--cursor);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .clue {
    margin: 4rem 0 0;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    opacity: 0.7;
    transform: rotate(-1.5deg);
  }

  .sections {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 5.5rem;
  }

  section {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 3rem;
  }

  .num {
    flex: 0 0 7.5rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 3.5rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--cursor);
  }

  .body {
    flex: 999 1 32.5rem;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 42.5rem;
  }

  .body h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.125rem;
    font-size: 1.875rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .body p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .editors {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .editor {
    flex: 1 1 16.25rem;
    padding: 1.375rem 1.375rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    transform: rotate(-0.6deg);
  }

  .editor + .editor {
    border-radius: 6px 3px 7px 4px;
    transform: rotate(0.8deg);
  }

  .editor p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .body .editor-name {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .nvim {
    color: var(--accent-0);
  }

  .emacs {
    color: var(--red);
  }

  del {
    text-decoration-line: line-through;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--red) 70%, transparent);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1.5px;
  }

  ins {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  ins.hand {
    margin-left: 0.25em;
    font-size: 1.15em;
    color: var(--red);
  }

  .body h2 del {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
  }

  .body h2 ins {
    display: block;
  }

  .recanted {
    color: var(--fg-dim);
  }

  .recanted del {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .retired {
    filter: grayscale(1);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .margin-note {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.75rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--red) 45%, transparent);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--red);
    transform: rotate(-0.8deg);
  }

  .dashes {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.875rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .dashes li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.875rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .dashes svg {
    flex: none;
  }

  .dashes path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--cursor);
    stroke-width: 2.2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  :global(.about-end) {
    margin: 5.5rem auto 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 47.99em) {
    .lede {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .sections {
      gap: 3.5rem;
    }

    .num {
      flex-basis: 100%;
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }

    .body h2 {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
